From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:24:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 097/144] GreatDANE: signer round 3: symlink escape, framework
 Current only, more owner guards, ad-hoc mode (NGD round 2 LOW)

sign_dane_macos.py:
- plan refuses any symlink inside the bundle that resolves outside it (file, directory or relative ../).
- Frameworks: only the CFBundleExecutable under the version that Versions/Current points at is exempt. A
  second real version's binary (e.g. Versions/B) has no row, so it's refused. If there's no Current link,
  a single real version is accepted.
- Owner guard (case-insensitive realpath):
  - also refuses /Applications and ~/Applications;
  - also refuses anything inside an attached disk image (`hdiutil info -plist`) whose image name contains
    "dane" or whose mount holds a top-level Dane.app (owner dmg on a custom mount point);
  - also refuses a Dane.app with an owner CFBundleIdentifier (surf.dogecoin.dane,
    org.mozilla.surf.pepecoin.greatdane) outside this tree unless --work-dir/DANE_SIGN_WORK_DIRS covers it.
- --allow-volume / DANE_SIGN_ALLOW_VOLUMES entries must be under /Volumes (and not bare /Volumes); a
  dangling entry elsewhere now gives rc 2.
- New `guard-path <path>...` subcommand: owner rules only, for sign-only.sh source/target paths.
- Ad-hoc mode for throwaway check runs: DANE_SIGN_IDENTITY=- signs with "-", without --timestamp and without
  the keychain, but keeps --options runtime and the per-binary entitlements.
  - `check` reports ad-hoc rows as "expected, not Developer ID" and prints CHECK PASS (AD-HOC ...).
  - --strict or DANE_SIGN_STRICT=1 makes ad-hoc fail; mixed ad-hoc/Developer ID always fails.
- Runtime detection now parses the CodeDirectory flags list, because ad-hoc prints 0x10002(adhoc,runtime).

Selftest: TEAM is read from greatdane/macos/signing.conf (no hard-coded team ID left). New cases G17-G31,
S1-S3, F1-F2, A1-A8; 67/67 pass in the scratch repo.
